1
00:00:05,490 --> 00:00:07,880
Hey, you guys. Hey, what are you doing?

2
00:00:07,930 --> 00:00:09,660
Figuring out our wedding plans.

3
00:00:09,710 --> 00:00:11,690
Funny. We were doing the same thing.

4
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:17,650
It's really crazy. The hall, the dress, the food.

5
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:20,240
I had no idea how expensive this was.

6
00:00:20,290 --> 00:00:21,500
Yeah, it is really pricey.

7
00:00:21,550 --> 00:00:23,390
I freaked when I heard the numbers.

8
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:24,880
So, what did you two do about it?

9
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:26,260
It was simple.

10
00:00:26,310 --> 00:00:28,390
I came up with some cost-cutting solutions...

11
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:31,110
...wrote out a list, and Monica told me to go to hell.

12
00:00:32,510 --> 00:00:33,930
There's no way around it.

13
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:36,730
Just accept that this is gonna cost a lot of money.

14
00:00:36,780 --> 00:00:40,240
I heard that weddings are, like, a $40 billion-a-year industry.

15
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:43,090
Yeah. And I'm responsible for just, like, half of that.

16
00:00:45,350 --> 00:00:48,920
But really, it does seem like this money could be put to better use.

17
00:00:48,920 --> 00:00:50,200
Are you serious?

18
00:00:50,250 --> 00:00:51,920
Yeah. How would you feel

19
00:00:51,970 --> 00:00:53,670
if we gave all the wedding money to charity...

20
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:56,090
...and we just got married at City Hall?

21
00:00:56,140 --> 00:00:58,880
I think it would make me wanna marry you even more.

22
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:04,660
I gotta say, you guys, that's an incredible gesture.

23
00:01:04,710 --> 00:01:06,850
Maybe you do that next time you get married.

24
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:12,460
No, no, no. The next time's gonna be Hawaii at sunset.

25
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:15,210
But maybe the time after that.

26
00:01:16,440 --> 00:01:18,530
Friends S10E07 The One With The Home Study

27
00:01:56,190 --> 00:01:58,680
- Hey. What's going on? - Hey.

28
00:01:58,820 --> 00:02:01,110
Our adoption social worker is coming,

29
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:02,690
so we're cleaning the apartment.

30
00:02:02,740 --> 00:02:03,750
"We"?

31
00:02:05,030 --> 00:02:06,960
You know you don't want me to help.

32
00:02:07,010 --> 00:02:08,940
You can't have it both ways.

33
00:02:10,350 --> 00:02:11,720
Is this the person who decides

34
00:02:11,770 --> 00:02:13,110
whether or not you get a baby?

35
00:02:13,160 --> 00:02:15,800
Kind of. She's coming by to interview us and see where we live.

36
00:02:15,850 --> 00:02:17,170
And it has to go perfectly,

37
00:02:17,220 --> 00:02:18,780
because if she doesn't like something about us

38
00:02:18,830 --> 00:02:19,860
she can keep us off

39
00:02:19,860 --> 00:02:21,230
every adoption list in the state.

40
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:22,610
Hey, maybe I should stop by.

41
00:02:22,720 --> 00:02:24,140
She could be a soap opera fan.

42
00:02:24,990 --> 00:02:26,020
It's very impressive

43
00:02:26,070 --> 00:02:27,750
when the little people know a celebrity.

44
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:30,620
"Little people"?

45
00:02:30,960 --> 00:02:32,000
"Celebrity."

46
00:02:33,810 --> 00:02:35,340
So I think I'm just about done here.

47
00:02:35,390 --> 00:02:38,400
Unless you have any bad stuff hidden somewhere,

48
00:02:38,450 --> 00:02:40,510
like porn or cigarettes?

49
00:02:40,910 --> 00:02:41,910
What?

50
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:45,830
- No. - Chandler.

51
00:02:48,930 --> 00:02:49,900
I don't,

52
00:02:49,950 --> 00:02:52,000
and I'm offended by the insinuation.

53
00:02:52,050 --> 00:02:55,600
So there's not a magazine under the couch...

54
00:02:55,650 --> 00:02:58,850
...or cigarettes taped to the back of the toilet tank...

55
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:01,170
...or a filthy video in the VCR?

56
00:03:02,510 --> 00:03:04,250
I'll admit to the cigarettes and magazine.

57
00:03:04,300 --> 00:03:05,980
But that tape is not mine.

58
00:03:06,370 --> 00:03:07,620
It isn't mine.

59
00:03:07,670 --> 00:03:09,440
I guess we'll never know whose it is.

60
00:03:18,140 --> 00:03:19,020
May I help you?

61
00:03:19,070 --> 00:03:20,250
Yes. We're here

62
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:22,930
to make a rather sizable donation to the children.

63
00:03:22,980 --> 00:03:24,640
Any contribution, large or small,

64
00:03:24,690 --> 00:03:25,640
is appreciated.

65
00:03:25,690 --> 00:03:27,030
I think you're gonna appreciate

66
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:28,480
the crap out of this one.

67
00:03:29,420 --> 00:03:30,950
Well, this is very generous.

68
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:32,630
And we don't want any recognition.

69
00:03:32,680 --> 00:03:34,520
This is completely anonymous.

70
00:03:34,570 --> 00:03:37,190
Completely anonymous. From two kind strangers.

71
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:39,700
Mr. X and Phoebe Buffay.

72
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:42,220
Well if you like,

73
00:03:42,270 --> 00:03:43,640
we can include your names in our newsletter.

74
00:03:43,690 --> 00:03:44,500
Not necessary.

75
00:03:44,550 --> 00:03:46,720
Buffay is spelled B-U-F-F-A-Y.

76
00:03:47,850 --> 00:03:51,300
And X is spelled "Mike Hannigan."

77
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:55,570
Well, on behalf of the children, thank you both very much.

78
00:03:55,570 --> 00:03:58,140
I'm glad we did this. It feels so good.

79
00:03:58,190 --> 00:03:59,660
It does. It feels really good.

80
00:04:00,510 --> 00:04:02,450
Oh, look. And we get these free T-shirts.

81
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:05,160
Actually, that's the shirt I wore to the gym.

82
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:08,480
It's moist.

83
00:04:11,530 --> 00:04:13,480
Hi. Emma will be up in a minute.

84
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:14,350
Oh, good.

85
00:04:14,350 --> 00:04:17,520
Hey, Ross, listen. I heard about you and Charlie.

86
00:04:17,570 --> 00:04:18,460
I'm really sorry.

87
00:04:18,510 --> 00:04:19,840
That's okay.

88
00:04:19,890 --> 00:04:23,140
I'm sure there are tons of other beautiful paleontologists out there.

89
00:04:23,190 --> 00:04:24,060
Absolutely.

90
00:04:24,110 --> 00:04:26,110
There was one. She's it.

91
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:29,180
All the rest look like they should live under a bridge.

92
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:33,880
So, what are you gonna do today?

93
00:04:33,930 --> 00:04:36,240
I was thinking of taking Emma to the playground.

94
00:04:36,290 --> 00:04:38,230
Oh, my God. What?

95
00:04:40,310 --> 00:04:41,700
Like I said, I was thinking of

96
00:04:41,750 --> 00:04:45,010
taking Emma to the Museum of Knives and Fire.

97
00:04:47,460 --> 00:04:48,850
Okay, look, Ross.

98
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:52,770
I do not want Emma going to the playground.

99
00:04:56,530 --> 00:04:57,760
Because...?

100
00:04:57,810 --> 00:05:01,190
All right, if you must know, I had a traumatic...

101
00:05:01,730 --> 00:05:04,700
...swing incident when I was little.

102
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:08,330
- Seriously? - Yes. I was 4 years old.

103
00:05:08,380 --> 00:05:10,050
And I was on the swing...

104
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:14,230
...and then all of a sudden my hair got tangled in the chain.

105
00:05:15,850 --> 00:05:16,780
And to get me out,

106
00:05:16,830 --> 00:05:19,920
my mom had to cut a big chunk of my hair.

107
00:05:22,140 --> 00:05:24,500
And it was uneven for weeks.

108
00:05:30,990 --> 00:05:33,000
And you made it through that?

109
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:37,710
I wonder who's gonna play you in the movie.

110
00:05:39,450 --> 00:05:41,070
Okay, fine, you can make fun of me.

111
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:43,220
I do not want Emma going there.

112
00:05:43,520 --> 00:05:45,740
And I was thinking Claire Danes.

113
00:05:47,030 --> 00:05:49,770
Look, I'm sorry to hear about your tragedy.

114
00:05:49,820 --> 00:05:52,020
But the swings are perfectly safe.

115
00:05:52,070 --> 00:05:53,520
And besides, Emma loves them.

116
00:05:53,570 --> 00:05:55,520
You should come, and you'll see.

117
00:05:55,570 --> 00:05:58,330
Those things go, like, 40 miles an hour.

118
00:05:58,950 --> 00:06:00,580
And there's that moment when you're at the top...

119
00:06:00,630 --> 00:06:04,960
...when you just don't know if you're gonna return back to Earth.

120
00:06:06,720 --> 00:06:09,700
Space is filled with orbiting children.

121
00:06:12,790 --> 00:06:15,340
Look, please, just come on.

122
00:06:15,390 --> 00:06:17,550
When you see the look on Emma's face,

123
00:06:17,600 --> 00:06:18,970
I swear, you won't regret it.

124
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:23,050
- All right. - Good.

125
00:06:23,100 --> 00:06:24,700
You don't wanna be a mom

126
00:06:24,750 --> 00:06:27,890
who passes her irrational fears to her children.

127
00:06:27,940 --> 00:06:29,470
"Irrational," huh?

128
00:06:29,750 --> 00:06:31,490
I'll remember that next time

129
00:06:31,540 --> 00:06:33,340
you freak out about a spider in your apartment.

130
00:06:33,390 --> 00:06:35,260
That's the same. I'm sure there are 30

131
00:06:35,310 --> 00:06:37,570
different species of poisonous swings.

132
00:06:42,090 --> 00:06:44,370
Oh, my God. The adoption lady is early.

133
00:06:44,420 --> 00:06:47,410
Okay. Okay. Here we go. Here we go.

134
00:06:47,850 --> 00:06:49,120
Stand up straight.

135
00:06:49,550 --> 00:06:50,740
Big smile.

136
00:06:53,660 --> 00:06:56,050
Hello. Is this the Creepy residence?

137
00:06:56,980 --> 00:06:58,730
We're waiting for the adoption lady.

138
00:06:58,780 --> 00:06:59,990
But I'm glad you're here.

139
00:07:00,040 --> 00:07:01,550
I was cleaning this morning

140
00:07:01,600 --> 00:07:03,050
and I found this.

141
00:07:03,380 --> 00:07:05,800
I don't know if you wanna use it, but....

142
00:07:06,370 --> 00:07:09,450
Oh, this is so sweet of you.

143
00:07:09,560 --> 00:07:10,680
But you know what?

144
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:11,800
I won't be needing a veil,

145
00:07:11,850 --> 00:07:13,560
I actually won't be wearing a dress at all!

146
00:07:13,610 --> 00:07:14,320
I told you,

147
00:07:14,370 --> 00:07:16,290
I am not coming to a naked wedding!

148
00:07:16,780 --> 00:07:19,170
No. We're not having a big reception.

149
00:07:19,220 --> 00:07:21,040
we took the money we were gonna spend on a wedding

150
00:07:21,090 --> 00:07:23,110
and we donate them to the children charity.

151
00:07:23,160 --> 00:07:24,720
That's crazy!

152
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:29,460
I'm sorry. I can't imagine giving up

153
00:07:29,460 --> 00:07:31,140
my one wedding day like that.

154
00:07:31,260 --> 00:07:32,500
Well, we're different.

155
00:07:32,540 --> 00:07:34,760
I don't care about having a huge party.

156
00:07:34,810 --> 00:07:37,210
This is really nice for you, but....

157
00:07:37,260 --> 00:07:40,970
Oh, please. I put this on and I just look like--

158
00:07:41,020 --> 00:07:42,220
Well, radiant.

159
00:07:45,150 --> 00:07:46,510
All right, but who cares?

160
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:49,270
I don't need a pretty veil and a fancy dress.

161
00:07:49,320 --> 00:07:51,610
That's right. You're making a commitment.

162
00:07:51,660 --> 00:07:54,810
You know, that's the same whether you do it at the Plaza or....

163
00:07:54,860 --> 00:07:57,030
- Where you gonna do it? - City Hall.

164
00:07:57,080 --> 00:08:01,280
Oh, that sounds nice.

165
00:08:02,100 --> 00:08:03,780
I was just there for jury duty.

166
00:08:03,830 --> 00:08:05,910
They've really spruced that place up.

167
00:08:06,410 --> 00:08:07,810
Okay. It's okay...

168
00:08:07,860 --> 00:08:10,920
I've made my decision.

169
00:08:11,220 --> 00:08:14,000
What I really want is a great big wedding.

170
00:08:16,260 --> 00:08:18,530
But you gave all the money to charity.

171
00:08:18,580 --> 00:08:20,340
Well, I'll just ask for it back.

172
00:08:22,130 --> 00:08:23,540
I don't think you can do that.

173
00:08:23,590 --> 00:08:24,510
Why not?

174
00:08:24,560 --> 00:08:25,430
This is her wedding day.

175
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:28,560
That's way more important than some stupid kids.

176
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:31,090
That's sweet, honey,

177
00:08:31,140 --> 00:08:33,260
but save something for the adoption lady.

178
00:08:40,150 --> 00:08:42,510
- All right, okay. Be careful. - Okay.

179
00:08:42,560 --> 00:08:45,550
Careful. Watch her hair. Watch her hair!

180
00:08:47,100 --> 00:08:49,130
Rach, she's got, like, three hairs.

181
00:08:49,180 --> 00:08:50,620
I know. I know.

182
00:08:50,670 --> 00:08:52,530
But they're just so beautiful.

183
00:08:52,580 --> 00:08:54,760
Oh, my God, I just pulled one out.

184
00:08:55,710 --> 00:08:57,400
I promise you she's safe.

185
00:08:57,450 --> 00:08:59,530
Watch how much she loves this.

186
00:08:59,580 --> 00:09:00,320
Okay. Okay.

187
00:09:00,370 --> 00:09:02,730
Are you ready, sweetie? Here we go.

188
00:09:04,290 --> 00:09:07,230
Okay, careful. Okay.

189
00:09:11,420 --> 00:09:13,130
She's smiling.

190
00:09:13,750 --> 00:09:15,940
Look at that, she does like it.

191
00:09:16,060 --> 00:09:17,760
See, I told you.

192
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:24,150
Oh, my God.

193
00:09:24,150 --> 00:09:26,770
Look at her, she's a little daredevil.

194
00:09:26,990 --> 00:09:29,230
Oh, God. Let me push. Can I push?

195
00:09:29,280 --> 00:09:31,080
Oh, absolutely.

196
00:09:31,540 --> 00:09:33,630
Oh, God. Okay, get the camera.

197
00:09:33,640 --> 00:09:35,130
It's in the diaper bag.

198
00:09:35,180 --> 00:09:36,280
Okay.

199
00:09:36,940 --> 00:09:39,260
See? Scared of the swings.

200
00:09:39,260 --> 00:09:40,800
I bet you feel pretty silly.

201
00:09:45,870 --> 00:09:47,940
We're asking for the money back?

202
00:09:47,990 --> 00:09:49,500
It's for our wedding day.

203
00:09:49,550 --> 00:09:51,650
Now, is this guy gay or straight?

204
00:09:51,700 --> 00:09:53,820
Because one of us has to start flirting.

205
00:09:55,420 --> 00:09:57,710
You here to make another donation the same day?

206
00:09:57,760 --> 00:09:59,650
I don't think that's ever happened before.

207
00:09:59,700 --> 00:10:01,130
Gay. Go.

208
00:10:04,590 --> 00:10:06,550
Oh, my God, I love your shirt.

209
00:10:08,750 --> 00:10:10,790
The donation we made earlier?

210
00:10:10,840 --> 00:10:13,360
Well, we want it back.

211
00:10:14,740 --> 00:10:15,660
Excuse me?

212
00:10:15,710 --> 00:10:18,420
Okay, that money was for a big wedding

213
00:10:18,470 --> 00:10:19,660
we thought we didn't want.

214
00:10:19,710 --> 00:10:21,160
But it turns out we do.

215
00:10:21,210 --> 00:10:22,500
So you're asking us

216
00:10:22,550 --> 00:10:24,770
to refund your donation to the children?

217
00:10:25,150 --> 00:10:26,040
Yeah.

218
00:10:27,970 --> 00:10:29,460
This feels really good.

219
00:10:33,540 --> 00:10:35,310
I'm sorry. I am.

220
00:10:35,360 --> 00:10:37,390
But this wedding's just really important to me.

221
00:10:37,560 --> 00:10:39,110
Hey, it's none of my business.

222
00:10:39,160 --> 00:10:41,350
Besides, this is probably a good thing.

223
00:10:41,400 --> 00:10:43,010
We've really been spoiling the children,

224
00:10:43,060 --> 00:10:44,960
what with all the food and warm clothing.

225
00:10:46,760 --> 00:10:48,130
That's not fair.

226
00:10:48,180 --> 00:10:49,890
A person's wedding is important.

227
00:10:49,940 --> 00:10:51,620
And especially to me.

228
00:10:51,670 --> 00:10:54,140
I didn't have a graduation party.

229
00:10:54,190 --> 00:10:55,620
And I didn't go to prom.

230
00:10:55,670 --> 00:10:59,680
And I spent my sweet 16 being chased around a tire yard...

231
00:10:59,730 --> 00:11:02,060
...by an escaped mental patient

232
00:11:02,110 --> 00:11:03,450
who, in his own words, wanted to:

233
00:11:03,500 --> 00:11:05,010
"Kill me, or whatever."

234
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:09,820
So I deserve a real celebration.

235
00:11:09,870 --> 00:11:12,760
And I'm not gonna let some sweaty little man

236
00:11:12,810 --> 00:11:14,610
make me feel badly about it.

237
00:11:18,680 --> 00:11:20,910
She could've been talking about either one of us.

238
00:11:27,830 --> 00:11:29,030
Hi, I'm Laura.

239
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:30,760
I'm here for your adoption interview.

240
00:11:30,810 --> 00:11:33,490
Hi, I'm Monica. And this is Chandler.

241
00:11:33,610 --> 00:11:35,890
- Please come in. - Thank you.

242
00:11:36,020 --> 00:11:37,400
Would you like something to drink?

243
00:11:37,450 --> 00:11:38,660
Water would be fine.

244
00:11:38,710 --> 00:11:41,380
We're so glad that you're here.

245
00:11:41,920 --> 00:11:44,540
We're excited about getting this process started.

246
00:11:44,590 --> 00:11:47,090
Because we love kids. Love them to death.

247
00:11:47,680 --> 00:11:49,620
Well, not actually to death.

248
00:11:49,670 --> 00:11:51,260
That's just a figure of speech.

249
00:11:51,310 --> 00:11:53,350
We love kids the appropriate amount...

250
00:11:55,100 --> 00:11:57,010
...as allowed by law.

251
00:11:59,240 --> 00:12:01,740
- Your place is just lovely. - Thank you.

252
00:12:01,790 --> 00:12:04,460
Yes, this building does have a wholesome,

253
00:12:04,460 --> 00:12:05,700
family feel to it.

254
00:12:05,870 --> 00:12:08,360
I feel like I've been here before.

255
00:12:08,410 --> 00:12:10,460
Any other couples in the building adopting?

256
00:12:10,510 --> 00:12:12,290
Is that that couple on the first floor?

257
00:12:12,340 --> 00:12:14,550
Because we should get a baby before them.

258
00:12:14,600 --> 00:12:17,090
That guy tried to sell me drugs.

259
00:12:18,430 --> 00:12:19,930
But other than that,

260
00:12:19,930 --> 00:12:21,610
wholesome, wholesome building.

261
00:12:24,490 --> 00:12:25,250
What?

262
00:12:25,470 --> 00:12:28,100
I realized why I remember this place.

263
00:12:28,150 --> 00:12:29,300
Really? What is it?

264
00:12:29,350 --> 00:12:30,330
Oh, it's nothing.

265
00:12:30,380 --> 00:12:32,160
I went on a date with a guy who lived in this building.

266
00:12:32,160 --> 00:12:34,240
It didn't end very well.

267
00:12:34,660 --> 00:12:37,990
That wouldn't, by any chance, be Joey Tribbiani?

268
00:12:38,030 --> 00:12:40,650
- Yes! - Of course it was.

269
00:12:41,750 --> 00:12:43,490
We had a great night.

270
00:12:43,490 --> 00:12:45,040
In the morning, he promised he'd call

271
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:46,120
and he didn't.

272
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:47,990
Rat bastard!

273
00:12:49,870 --> 00:12:50,870
So you're not friends with him?

274
00:12:50,870 --> 00:12:51,800
Oh, God, no.

275
00:12:51,800 --> 00:12:53,010
No, no, no.

276
00:12:53,010 --> 00:12:54,540
No. Nope.

277
00:12:54,540 --> 00:12:55,400
No...

278
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:56,080
No...

279
00:12:56,080 --> 00:12:56,820
No...

280
00:12:56,820 --> 00:12:57,450
No...

281
00:12:59,040 --> 00:12:59,670
No...

282
00:13:02,350 --> 00:13:04,540
Well, I'm sorry I brought it up.

283
00:13:04,540 --> 00:13:07,910
So are either one of you planning on staying at home?

284
00:13:08,090 --> 00:13:12,480
Hello? Anybody in there order a celebrity?

285
00:13:16,180 --> 00:13:17,670
What was that?

286
00:13:17,670 --> 00:13:20,660
That's just some crazy guy who roams the halls here.

287
00:13:21,490 --> 00:13:23,450
He's great with kids, though.

288
00:13:30,460 --> 00:13:32,880
Ross. Oh, my God, are you okay?

289
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:34,500
Son of a bitch!

290
00:13:38,630 --> 00:13:41,330
Oh, relax. I didn't say the F-word.

291
00:13:43,560 --> 00:13:44,250
Ross, see,

292
00:13:44,250 --> 00:13:46,610
I told you! Those swings are evil!

293
00:13:46,660 --> 00:13:47,930
That is it.

294
00:13:47,980 --> 00:13:49,510
That's the last time Emma is getting on

295
00:13:49,560 --> 00:13:51,370
one of those things for her entire life.

296
00:13:51,490 --> 00:13:54,110
No, no, no. Okay, it wasn't the swing's fault.

297
00:13:54,160 --> 00:13:55,430
It was my fault.

298
00:13:55,480 --> 00:13:57,770
And kind of that kid's fault.

299
00:13:58,430 --> 00:14:01,460
Who is still laughing. Nice.

300
00:14:01,940 --> 00:14:03,850
Come on. Can we just get out of here

301
00:14:03,900 --> 00:14:05,400
before somebody else gets hurt?

302
00:14:05,450 --> 00:14:07,380
No. Wait. Ok, ok. I have an idea.

303
00:14:07,430 --> 00:14:09,020
I want you to get on the swing...

304
00:14:09,070 --> 00:14:12,460
...and you'll see that there's nothing to be afraid of.

305
00:14:15,070 --> 00:14:16,920
I know what this is all about.

306
00:14:18,010 --> 00:14:20,240
You've always been jealous of my hair.

307
00:14:21,500 --> 00:14:23,700
I just think you're an adult, okay?

308
00:14:23,750 --> 00:14:25,840
And you should get over your silly fears.

309
00:14:25,890 --> 00:14:27,880
All right, fine. I'll do it.

310
00:14:27,930 --> 00:14:28,530
Good.

311
00:14:28,580 --> 00:14:29,610
If you hold a spider.

312
00:14:29,660 --> 00:14:31,000
Where?! Where?!

313
00:14:32,160 --> 00:14:34,430
If you hold a spider.

314
00:14:34,830 --> 00:14:35,930
I know.

315
00:14:43,550 --> 00:14:45,160
Guys, is everything okay?

316
00:14:45,310 --> 00:14:46,740
It's me, Joey.

317
00:14:48,950 --> 00:14:50,400
Adoption!

318
00:14:52,550 --> 00:14:53,720
What's going on?

319
00:14:53,840 --> 00:14:56,340
Oh, it's just like I said, that crazy...

320
00:14:56,930 --> 00:14:59,730
...Bert, roaming the halls.

321
00:15:00,680 --> 00:15:01,430
Guys?

322
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:02,960
Keep on roaming, Bert!

323
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:06,940
We don't want any crazy today!

324
00:15:07,410 --> 00:15:08,380
What's going on?

325
00:15:08,380 --> 00:15:10,950
We'll talk later! Bert. Everything's fine!

326
00:15:12,040 --> 00:15:14,040
Everything doesn't sound fine.

327
00:15:14,880 --> 00:15:16,690
Is he all right out there by himself?

328
00:15:16,690 --> 00:15:18,140
Oh, yeah. He has a caretaker.

329
00:15:18,140 --> 00:15:19,460
His older brother...

330
00:15:20,570 --> 00:15:22,040
...Ernie.

331
00:15:24,380 --> 00:15:25,860
Bert and Ernie?

332
00:15:25,860 --> 00:15:28,260
You can't make this stuff up.

333
00:15:30,120 --> 00:15:31,580
You never told me about that guy

334
00:15:31,580 --> 00:15:33,090
and your sweet 16.

335
00:15:33,090 --> 00:15:34,620
I'm sorry about that.

336
00:15:34,620 --> 00:15:36,160
Oh, it ended okay.

337
00:15:36,160 --> 00:15:38,010
One of my friends shot him.

338
00:15:39,950 --> 00:15:42,560
At least you'll get a proper wedding.

339
00:15:42,560 --> 00:15:43,550
You really deserve that.

340
00:15:43,550 --> 00:15:45,010
Yeah, I really do.

341
00:15:45,010 --> 00:15:47,210
You know, I had nothing growing up.

342
00:15:49,950 --> 00:15:52,410
Just like the kids I took the money from.

343
00:15:52,680 --> 00:15:55,460
No... I see where this is going.

344
00:15:55,460 --> 00:15:57,420
Don't make me go back there.

345
00:15:58,680 --> 00:16:01,440
Look, I can't have a wedding with this money now.

346
00:16:01,490 --> 00:16:02,690
It's tainted.

347
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:05,630
Fine, we'll give the money back.

348
00:16:05,680 --> 00:16:06,900
If that guy at the charity

349
00:16:06,950 --> 00:16:08,110
gives us a hard time...

350
00:16:08,160 --> 00:16:11,310
...my friend hasn't shot anyone in a really long time.

351
00:16:13,200 --> 00:16:15,050
I must say this seems like

352
00:16:15,050 --> 00:16:16,900
a lovely environment to raise a child in.

353
00:16:16,950 --> 00:16:19,180
You are welcome to look under

354
00:16:19,180 --> 00:16:20,170
any of the furniture...

355
00:16:20,220 --> 00:16:21,230
...because, believe me,

356
00:16:21,280 --> 00:16:23,640
you won't find any porn or cigarettes under there.

357
00:16:24,730 --> 00:16:26,250
Before we look around,

358
00:16:26,300 --> 00:16:27,620
let me make sure

359
00:16:27,620 --> 00:16:28,660
I have everything I need up to here.

360
00:16:34,970 --> 00:16:37,130
Why don't I show you the baby's room.

361
00:16:42,410 --> 00:16:43,720
What are you doing?

362
00:16:43,770 --> 00:16:44,720
You wouldn't let me in.

363
00:16:44,770 --> 00:16:45,960
I thought you were in trouble.

364
00:16:46,010 --> 00:16:46,840
Well, we're not.

365
00:16:46,890 --> 00:16:48,210
But you called me "Bert."

366
00:16:49,910 --> 00:16:51,730
That's our code word for danger.

367
00:16:53,140 --> 00:16:55,040
We don't have a code word.

368
00:16:55,090 --> 00:16:55,780
We don't?

369
00:16:57,230 --> 00:16:58,350
We really should.

370
00:16:58,980 --> 00:16:59,790
From now on,

371
00:16:59,840 --> 00:17:02,320
"Bert" will be our code word for danger.

372
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:05,320
So that was the baby's room.

373
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:08,920
What room should we see next?

374
00:17:08,970 --> 00:17:11,220
Any room that isn't behind this couch.

375
00:17:13,630 --> 00:17:15,110
Some people don't get him,

376
00:17:15,160 --> 00:17:16,880
but I think he's really funny.

377
00:17:24,680 --> 00:17:26,490
I did not care for that.

378
00:17:28,180 --> 00:17:29,380
You have to leave.

379
00:17:29,430 --> 00:17:31,130
You slept with our social worker

380
00:17:31,180 --> 00:17:32,310
and never called her back.

381
00:17:32,360 --> 00:17:33,430
She is still pissed,

382
00:17:33,480 --> 00:17:34,470
so she can't see you.

383
00:17:34,520 --> 00:17:36,000
Okay, okay.

384
00:17:39,340 --> 00:17:41,750
- What? - I forgot my bat.

385
00:17:44,900 --> 00:17:46,500
Oh, my God.

386
00:17:47,110 --> 00:17:48,380
And for the last time,

387
00:17:48,430 --> 00:17:50,930
we do not want to be friends with you!

388
00:17:53,520 --> 00:17:55,460
And we don't wanna buy your bat!

389
00:17:57,770 --> 00:17:59,420
What are you doing here?

390
00:17:59,740 --> 00:18:01,590
Bert...

391
00:18:06,070 --> 00:18:07,460
Are you friends with him?

392
00:18:07,510 --> 00:18:08,700
I can explain.

393
00:18:10,210 --> 00:18:11,210
Joey?

394
00:18:12,580 --> 00:18:14,030
All right. Okay.

395
00:18:18,660 --> 00:18:22,260
You have got some nerve coming back here.

396
00:18:23,190 --> 00:18:24,990
I can't believe you never called me.

397
00:18:24,990 --> 00:18:26,780
Excuse me?

398
00:18:27,240 --> 00:18:28,850
You probably don't even remember my name.

399
00:18:28,850 --> 00:18:30,450
It's Joey, by the way.

400
00:18:30,450 --> 00:18:31,620
And don't bother telling me yours,

401
00:18:31,620 --> 00:18:34,710
because I totally remember it, lady.

402
00:18:37,870 --> 00:18:39,400
I waited weeks for you to call me.

403
00:18:39,400 --> 00:18:40,480
I gave you my number.

404
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:41,490
You never called me.

405
00:18:41,540 --> 00:18:43,590
Don't try to turn this around on me.

406
00:18:43,640 --> 00:18:47,730
I am not some kind of social work...

407
00:18:47,780 --> 00:18:49,700
...that you can just...

408
00:18:49,750 --> 00:18:50,850
...do.

409
00:18:54,310 --> 00:18:56,770
I'm pretty sure I gave you my number.

410
00:18:56,820 --> 00:18:58,940
Really? Think about it. Come on.

411
00:18:58,990 --> 00:19:00,610
You're a beautiful woman.

412
00:19:00,660 --> 00:19:02,230
Smart, funny.

413
00:19:02,640 --> 00:19:04,790
We had a really good time.

414
00:19:06,660 --> 00:19:07,700
If I had your number,

415
00:19:07,750 --> 00:19:08,960
why wouldn't I call you?

416
00:19:09,970 --> 00:19:10,980
I don't know.

417
00:19:13,170 --> 00:19:14,430
Well, maybe I'm wrong.

418
00:19:14,480 --> 00:19:15,170
I'm sorry.

419
00:19:15,220 --> 00:19:18,830
Hey, too late for apologies. Okay?

420
00:19:18,880 --> 00:19:20,490
You broke my heart.

421
00:19:20,540 --> 00:19:21,470
You know how many women

422
00:19:21,520 --> 00:19:22,780
I had to sleep with to get over you?

423
00:19:27,220 --> 00:19:28,870
- Joey, wait-- - No!

424
00:19:29,540 --> 00:19:30,600
I waited a long time!

425
00:19:30,650 --> 00:19:31,950
I can't wait anymore.

426
00:19:35,920 --> 00:19:37,950
I'm sorry that you had to see that.

427
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:38,970
I'm so embarrassed.

428
00:19:39,020 --> 00:19:40,260
Oh, that's really okay.

429
00:19:40,310 --> 00:19:42,490
Yeah. We totally understand.

430
00:19:42,540 --> 00:19:43,880
Dating is hard.

431
00:19:44,380 --> 00:19:46,200
Boy, you people are nice.

432
00:19:47,850 --> 00:19:49,410
And I've got to say...

433
00:19:49,770 --> 00:19:53,020
...l think you're going to make excellent parents.

434
00:19:57,050 --> 00:19:58,420
Laura!

435
00:20:05,700 --> 00:20:06,870
We're back.

436
00:20:08,430 --> 00:20:10,080
Are you here to take more money?

437
00:20:10,990 --> 00:20:13,350
Because I think what you're looking for is an ATM.

438
00:20:14,260 --> 00:20:16,430
No, no, we're here to give the money back.

439
00:20:16,480 --> 00:20:18,170
Yeah. Because you know what?

440
00:20:18,860 --> 00:20:20,570
It's all about the children.

441
00:20:20,620 --> 00:20:23,370
Although it's also about the wedding.

442
00:20:24,630 --> 00:20:25,710
All right, here.

443
00:20:25,810 --> 00:20:27,190
No. Oh, God.

444
00:20:27,240 --> 00:20:28,730
If I haven't said so already,

445
00:20:28,780 --> 00:20:30,360
sir, congratulations.

446
00:20:31,660 --> 00:20:33,710
Enough, all right?

447
00:20:33,710 --> 00:20:35,710
I'm stepping in and putting my foot down.

448
00:20:35,760 --> 00:20:36,540
As your future husband,

449
00:20:36,540 --> 00:20:39,270
I'm gonna make this decision for us.

450
00:20:40,340 --> 00:20:42,810
What do you think we should do?

451
00:20:43,570 --> 00:20:46,250
You know what. It's not your decision anymore.

452
00:20:46,250 --> 00:20:46,880
What?

453
00:20:46,880 --> 00:20:48,570
On behalf of the children of New York,

454
00:20:48,570 --> 00:20:50,340
I reject your money.

455
00:20:51,210 --> 00:20:52,530
But we're giving you this.

456
00:20:52,530 --> 00:20:54,240
And I'm giving it back to you.

457
00:20:54,240 --> 00:20:56,800
Come on. Consider it a contribution.

458
00:20:58,450 --> 00:21:00,690
Well, this is very generous.

459
00:21:01,360 --> 00:21:02,410
Please take the check.

460
00:21:02,410 --> 00:21:03,400
Have a great wedding

461
00:21:03,400 --> 00:21:05,470
and a wonderful life together.

462
00:21:05,550 --> 00:21:07,000
Sounds good to me.

463
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:08,900
We can save up, come back in a few years...

464
00:21:08,900 --> 00:21:10,200
...and make an even bigger donation.

465
00:21:10,200 --> 00:21:12,950
Absolutely. And when you do, make sure you ask for Brian.

466
00:21:12,950 --> 00:21:14,740
- Oh, is that you? - No.

467
00:21:20,220 --> 00:21:21,100
Hello?

468
00:21:22,520 --> 00:21:23,670
Oh, hi.

469
00:21:25,240 --> 00:21:27,430
Oh, my God, really?

470
00:21:27,480 --> 00:21:29,280
I can't wait to tell Chandler.

471
00:21:29,330 --> 00:21:30,670
Okay. Goodbye.

472
00:21:31,550 --> 00:21:32,770
Wrong number?

473
00:21:33,550 --> 00:21:34,740
That was Laura.

474
00:21:35,380 --> 00:21:36,700
She gave us a great report

475
00:21:36,750 --> 00:21:38,690
and we're officially on the waiting list.

476
00:21:38,740 --> 00:21:39,640
That's great.

477
00:21:39,690 --> 00:21:40,770
Now we just wait for a call...

478
00:21:40,820 --> 00:21:42,150
...and someone tells us

479
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:43,860
there's a baby waiting for us.

480
00:21:57,300 --> 00:21:58,230
Hello?

481
00:21:59,380 --> 00:22:00,740
Have you seen Joey's bat?

482
00:22:07,350 --> 00:22:10,000
Okay. I got a spider.

483
00:22:10,390 --> 00:22:12,220
There were two, I picked the bigger one.

484
00:22:13,940 --> 00:22:15,800
- Okay. - Okay.

485
00:22:19,870 --> 00:22:22,130
This feels perfectly normal.

486
00:22:23,160 --> 00:22:24,960
Okay, get on the swing.

487
00:22:27,440 --> 00:22:28,720
Okay.

488
00:22:29,990 --> 00:22:32,390
Okay.

489
00:22:38,060 --> 00:22:39,040
Okay.

490
00:22:47,030 --> 00:22:47,920
See?

491
00:22:47,970 --> 00:22:50,200
All right. I can do this.

492
00:22:50,250 --> 00:22:52,260
There you go. Good for you.

493
00:22:52,310 --> 00:22:54,710
You know what? I'm getting used to this little guy.

494
00:22:54,760 --> 00:22:57,130
I don't even feel him in here anymore.

495
00:22:57,180 --> 00:22:58,790
That's because he's on your neck.

